    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d126">

                <pb facs="0352" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1436</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 6, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>179. Believe Italian Government inclined to think German order declaring war zone
                    about British Isles threatening neutral vessels requires some observations. Am
                    informally asked what our Government proposes to do. This believed to be with
                    view of having [action] on parallel lines.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
